      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731637736753,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now since both get and post route point to  the same endpoint ideally what should happen\nis the html page which GET/ route shows should get rendered with the data sent from server \nvia the POST route/ as both points to the same endpoint but in reality when we hit \n\nsubmit button -client sents a post request via form  to express server and express \nserver a send a new html page with the processed data  ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now since both get and post route point to  the same endpoint ideally what should happen\nis the html page which GET/ route shows should get rendered with the data sent from server \nvia the POST route/ as both points to the same endpoint but in reality when we hit \n\nsubmit button -client sents a post request via form  to express server and express \nserver a send a new html page with the processed data  ",
